# observation — a mind may decline once, and asked again it must attend
#
# A click on a kind asks the mind chosen to look at one thing of that kind, of its own choosing —
# or to say that nothing there draws it. The declining costs its point like any observation, stands
# on the map as a refusal, and is spent: the same mind asked again about the same kind in the same
# area has to attend to something. Another mind still has its own declining.
#
# --refuse-focus stands in for the choice judge answering "nothing here", which --playground never
# does: it forces the decline wherever one is allowed.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --refuse-focus

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# Childhood Memory is asked to look at a thing, and declines.
click observe thing
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state texts "Nothing here draws my attention"
expect-state trees refusal area="Test Yard" mind=childhood_memory
expect-no-state trees element
expect-state noetic points=2/3

# Asked again, it may not: something is observed.
click observe thing
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element
expect-state trees observer=childhood_memory
expect-state noetic points=1/3

# Another mind has a declining of its own.
click observe thing
choose comradeship
advance 12 180
expect-state trees refusal area="Test Yard" mind=comradeship
quit
